			<p class="kicker">Static sites, with a sense of humor</p>
			<h1>Large, quick, and rarely photographed.</h1>
			<p class="lead">SiteSquatch (<code>ssqch</code>) turns your Markdown and templates into a website, and it's good company while it works. Break a link or misspell a field, and it names the file and the line, takes a guess at what you meant, and might crack a dry joke about it. The jokes stay in your terminal. Your site gets plain HTML.</p>
			<div class="actions">
