<section class="first-minute" aria-labelledby="first-minute">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div>
			<p class="kicker">Your first minute</p>
			<h2 id="first-minute">Two commands, and you've got a website</h2>
			<p><code>ssqch init</code> sets up camp: a config, a layout, a home page, five posts, a 404 page, a blueprint for the next post, editor types, and an <code>AGENTS.md</code> for your coding agent. Then it leaves you to it. Run <code>ssqch serve</code>, edit a post, and the page you're looking at reloads.</p>
			<p><a href="{{ links.fieldGuide }}">The field guide walks you through it</a></p>
		</div>
		<figure class="terminal">
			<figcaption class="terminal-bar">Terminal</figcaption>
<pre><span class="p">$</span> npx ssqch init my-site
<span class="c">  ...</span>
<span class="v">Camp is set up.</span> Next: cd my-site &amp;&amp; ssqch serve, then open http://localhost:8080
<span class="p">$</span> cd my-site &amp;&amp; npx ssqch serve
<span class="v">First confirmed siting.</span> Built in 24.7 ms (development)
  Pages   7 written from 7 templates, 18.4 KB (7 changed)
  Links   14 checked, 0 broken
<span class="c">  ...</span>
Serving dist at http://localhost:8080/. <span class="v">Squatch Watch is on.</span>
<span class="v">Fresh tracks</span> in src/posts/i-know-what-i-saw.md
Built in 5.64 ms (development)
  Pages   7 written from 7 templates, 18.4 KB (1 changed)</pre>
		</figure>
	</div>
</section>

