<section class="stop" id="pack" aria-labelledby="pack-title">
	<div class="mile" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
	<div class="stop-head">
		<div>
			<p class="kicker">Mile 1 · What's in the pack</p>
			<h2 id="pack-title">A blog or a docs site, with no plugin hunt</h2>
			<p>The things every content site ends up needing are already in there, and each one is a line of config. Your config runs on Node, so anything that's missing is an npm package away.</p>
		</div>
		{{ drawing("stickers/backpack", 104, class="stop-art") }}
	</div>
	<ul class="pack">
		<li>{{ drawing("stickers/compass", 58) }}<div><h3>Templates you already know</h3><p>Jinja is the default. Edge, Liquid, Nunjucks, Handlebars, Mustache and EJS work too, so the templates you have can come along.</p></div></li>
		<li>{{ drawing("stickers/lantern", 58) }}<div><h3>Markdown that replaces a plugin stack</h3><p>Heading ids, footnotes, containers, render hooks in any template language, and syntax highlighting at build time.</p></div></li>
		<li>{{ drawing("stickers/raccoon", 58) }}<div><h3>Images, encoded once</h3><p>Every <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> becomes a <code>&lt;picture&gt;</code> with AVIF, WebP and a fallback, cached by content so later builds skip the encoding.</p></div></li>
		<li>{{ drawing("stickers/ranger-mary", 58) }}<div><h3>Checks on every build</h3><p>Content schemas for front matter and a link checker, so a typo fails the build and names the file, the field and a guess at the fix.</p></div></li>
		<li>{{ drawing("stickers/coffee", 58) }}<div><h3>A config that's plain JavaScript</h3><p>Filters, data, collections, transforms and build hooks, plus any npm package, <code>fetch</code> with a cache, and every Node built-in.</p></div></li>
		<li>{{ drawing("stickers/beaver", 58) }}<div><h3>A dev server that's careful</h3><p>Squatch Watch reloads only the page you changed, swaps stylesheets in place, and shows a broken build in the browser.</p></div></li>
	</ul>
	<p class="also">Also in the pack: themes without a package manager, custom elements that load only where they're used, Sass (yes, Sassquatch), a sitemap, redirects, RSS helpers, HTML minification and asset fingerprinting. <a href="{{ links.pack }}">The whole inventory</a></p>
</section>

<section class="stop" id="checks" aria-labelledby="checks-title">
	<div class="mile" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
	<div class="stop-head">
		<div>
			<p class="kicker">Mile 2 · Evidence</p>
			<h2 id="checks-title">When something's wrong, it points at the spot</h2>
			<p>A build that succeeds isn't proof that your site is fine. ssqch checks the things generators usually leave to you, reports every problem in one go, and takes a guess at what you meant.</p>
		</div>
		{{ drawing("stickers/footprint", 70, class="stop-art") }}
	</div>
	<div class="two-up">
		<div>
			<h3>Front matter, checked against a schema</h3>
			<p>A misspelled key, a date that isn't one, a hero image that was renamed. Each one gets its file and its line.</p>
			<figure class="terminal">
				<figcaption class="terminal-bar">ssqch build</figcaption>
<pre><span class="e">error:</span> 3 content errors:
  - src/posts/cedar.md: `status` must be "draft" or "published", not "drfat" (schema `posts`)
  - src/posts/cedar.md: `hero.src` is "cedar.jpg", but there's no such file next to the page (schema `posts`)
  - src/posts/cedar.md: `descripton` isn't a field of this schema (did you mean `description`?) (schema `posts`)

  --&gt; src/posts/cedar.md:5
   3 | date: 2026-03-02
   4 | tags: posts
   5 | status: drfat
     | <span class="v">^^^^^^</span>
   6 | hero: { src: cedar.jpg, alt: A cedar }</pre>
			</figure>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3>What a change did to the output</h3>
			<p>Upgrade ssqch, edit a layout or move from another generator, then compare the two builds. It's better evidence than most sightings get.</p>
			<figure class="terminal">
				<figcaption class="terminal-bar">ssqch diff before after</figcaption>
<pre><span class="c">...</span>
Added (1)
  <span class="a">+ /trails/cedar/</span>

Changed (1)
  ~ /trails/  (text and markup)
      ids removed (links to them break): #old-growth
      <span class="r">- &lt;h2 id="old-growth"&gt;</span>
      <span class="r">- Old growth</span>
      <span class="a">+ &lt;h2 id="cedar"&gt;</span>
      <span class="a">+ Cedar</span>

Changes found: 2 pages (1 changed, 1 added, 0 removed); 5 pages and 1 other file are the same. <span class="v">The stump has moved.</span></pre>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

