<section class="stop" id="agents" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
	<div class="mile" aria-hidden="true">6</div>
	<div class="stop-head">
		<div>
			<p class="kicker">Mile 6 · For coding agents</p>
			<h2 id="agents-title">The docs travel with the package</h2>
			<p>If a coding agent is doing the building, it doesn't need this website. The documentation ships inside ssqch, so the answer matches the version that's installed and needs no network.</p>
		</div>
		{{ drawing("stickers/owl", 104, class="stop-art") }}
	</div>
	<div class="with-terminal">
		<div>
			<p>Commands that report take <code>--format json</code>: a <code>schemaVersion</code>, diagnostic codes, and no jokes. <code>ssqch init</code> writes a 1 KB <code>AGENTS.md</code> that says where to look.</p>
			<p>Reading from the web instead? Every docs page has a Markdown copy at its address with <code>.md</code> on the end, a request that asks for <code>text/markdown</code> gets it, and <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> lists them all.</p>
			<p><a href="{{ links.agents }}">Scripts and coding agents</a></p>
		</div>
		<figure class="terminal">
			<figcaption class="terminal-bar">No browser required</figcaption>
<pre><span class="c"># One name, from the installed package</span>
<span class="p">$</span> ssqch docs base
<span class="c"># Another generator's words, with ssqch's for each</span>
<span class="p">$</span> ssqch docs --from eleventy
<span class="c"># What this version can do, and what a build did</span>
<span class="p">$</span> ssqch capabilities --format json
<span class="p">$</span> ssqch build --format json
<span class="c"># Or from the web, as Markdown</span>
<span class="p">$</span> curl https://sitesquatch.dev/docs/content-schemas.md</pre>
		</figure>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="stop" id="gaps" aria-labelledby="gaps-title">
	<div class="mile" aria-hidden="true">7</div>
	<div class="stop-head">
		<div>
			<p class="kicker">Mile 7 · The uncharted parts of the map</p>
			<h2 id="gaps-title">What it doesn't do yet</h2>
			<p>SiteSquatch is a young one (0.x), so expect some breaking changes between minor versions. Each is in the changelog with what you'd need to change. Some of the map is still blank, too:</p>
		</div>
		{{ drawing("stickers/mountain", 104, class="stop-art") }}
	</div>
	<ul class="gaps">
		<li>Pages render one at a time on one thread. Image encoding uses every core, but heavy per-page JavaScript doesn't spread across them.</li>
		<li>The dev server rebuilds the whole site on a change: about 0.9 s after one edit on a 10,000-page site.</li>
		<li>The dev server listens on <code>127.0.0.1</code> only. There's no <code>--host</code>.</li>
		<li>No SVG rasterizing, and HDR photos need converting to sRGB first (the build warns about them).</li>
	</ul>
	<p class="also"><a href="{{ links.knownGaps }}">Every known gap, as of this release</a></p>
</section>

